        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/4/p/midleton-wp/12-09-16-midleton-2602-2601-30.jpg",
          "filename": "12.09.16 Midleton 2602+2601 (30007966655).jpg",
          "caption": "Iarnród Éireann (Irish Rail) 2-car DMU no. 2602 with 2601 behind is seen at Midleton on 12 September 2016 on train P280, 12:45 Midletonto Cork Kent. This line originally from Youghal closed to passenger traffic in 1963 with freight being withdrawn by 1982. The line however remained in situ for the occasional special until 1988. With the upsurge in commuter traffic in the area, in 2009 the line re-opened again to passenger from here, Midleton. A basic hourly service is provided with additional trains during the morning and evening peak.",
          "alt": "Iarnród Éireann (Irish Rail) 2-car DMU no. 2602 with 2601 behind is seen at Midleton on 12 September 2016 on train P280, 12:45 Midletonto Cork Kent. This line originally from Youghal closed to passenger traffic in 1963 with freight being withdrawn by 1982. The line however remained in situ for the occasional special until 1988. With the upsurge in commuter traffic in the area, in 2009 the line re-opened again to passenger from here, Midleton. A basic hourly service is provided with additional trains during the morning and evening peak.",
          "width": 5312,
          "height": 3164,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Phil Richards from London, UK",
